  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A request passed to SendAsync and answered 401 is now sent again after renewal: SendAsync used to resend the same HttpRequestMessage, which .NET refuses, so the retry always threw InvalidOperationException. The retry now sends a copy carrying the headers and options the caller set and the same content object, which is not buffered; a StreamContent over a seekable stream is rewound to where it started, and one over a stream that cannot seek makes the retry throw HttpRequestException, with the consumed stream's InvalidOperationException as InnerException, instead of sending an empty body. The first 401 response is disposed, a 401 after renewal is returned, and GetAsync and PostAsync send through SendAsync with the HttpClient's default HTTP version. Adds AuthorizedHttpClient.IsRefusalStatus, the public refusal rule the client judges sign-in and refresh answers by, and makes HttpStatusText public, the way the client's messages word a status. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-client-v2.1.0/EasyReasy.Auth.Client/README.md#from-200",
